# 2019 onwards - return to Prime Ministerial government?

---
## Johnson
 
- Johnson's style combined with his 80-seat majority after the 2019 general election
- But then he is undermined by the resignations of 44 ministers

---
## Truss

- Using patronage to appoint loyal supports to Cabinet
- Introduced "Trussonomics"
- But: this quasi-presidential style of leadership was her downfall. Key [[MP]]s, free from collective responsibility because she didn't put them in the Cabinet (E.g. Gove) undermined her 

---
## Sunak

- Appointed a more balanced cabinet
- Weak party [[mandate]] because unopposed in leadership race
- Sunak's cabinet committees reflect a preference for small strategy meetings and the power of Jeremy Hunt
